WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Before I ask you about
"American Idol,"

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:02.802 line:92%
I want to congratulate you.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nominated for
Entertainer of the Year again.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.772 size:84% position:42%
-Yes, yes. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you come from
a very supportive community

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.175 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in country music.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you find -- are you
a supportive judge on "Idol"?

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that where
you come at it from?

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.581 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, it's interesting.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.281 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know, when you --

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody wants to know, well,
who's the mean one?

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who is the one that --
that just tears them apart,

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.323 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but you know, we all --

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
being artists, I think,
you know, we've all been there

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
and heard rejection and "no"
and the motivating --

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:35.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
the motivating sounds of "no"
as an artist.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:39.839
And so, when we're dealing with
these kids, we --

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.408 line:92%
you know, we're very truthful.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.375 line:92%
And I've even walked off set

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:45.378
and some of the people backstage
that watch the monitors,

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, all of the people
back there.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've got them. But anyway.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they were like,
"You are really --

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were kind of stern
with them."

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like --
and I didn't even realize it

00:00:55.955 --> 00:01:01.895
because I was caught up in
trying to really give them good,

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.196 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you know, good advice.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.699
You know, to carry them -- to
carry them, you know, far down

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
the road in music,
and it is interesting.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.538 line:92%
You know, a lot of these kids --

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I've lied awake
at night wondering,

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Gosh, did we make the right
decision on so-and-so?"

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's really,
really important.

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, a lot of these
kids, we may --

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.083 line:92%
we're not gonna bat 1.000.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:23.683 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We're not gonna --

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.019
We get caught up in the emotion
of it all, too,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we have to make decisions
pretty fast.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.724
I mean, we've got to cut them
to 100 to 50 to -- you know?

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:35.495
But, you know, these kids -- I'm
trying to land the plane here --

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:38.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
but these kids, you know,
they may go on --

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.132 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.167 size:88% position:44%
These kids will go on,
and even if we cut them,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.803 size:84% position:42%
they'll still work hard
and get record deals.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:46.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Had you been a contestant
back in the day,

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.440 size:88% position:44% line:92%
when you were their age,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.776
how do you think would you have
come through?

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.012
-I would have been the "aw,
shucks" gullible country boy

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
that could -- that could sing
a little bit,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:59.152
but I would have had to lean on
my charming personality.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:01:59.719 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My wit.
-Yeah.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.490
You probably would have brought
a dead alligator

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.424 line:92%
to prove you can do that.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:06.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I would have proved
that ability.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.894 line:92%
But the main thing with me is

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:11.131 size:84% position:42%
I wouldn't have known
who I was as an artist.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:15.001
I think -- We've got one --
we've got one girl that's --

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:18.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's going through
the high rounds and, you know,

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:22.408
she's 18 years old and she knows
exactly who she is...

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's crazy.
-...as an artist.

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:28.414
I mean, if you sent her a song,
the most obscure song,

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.749 line:92%
she would turn it into hers.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's not the best singer
in the world.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:35.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's not the best, you know,
musician in the world,

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.422 line:92%
but she is such an artist,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.559
we can't get enough of her,
and I wouldn't have had that.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:43.229
I was still trying to sing like
all my heroes at the time.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:43.730 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, sure.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, that's nice when people
can figure it out early.

